Since \(x>0\), its square root is real and satisfies \((\sqrt{x})^2=x\). Thus the expression inside the cube root is a perfect cube:
\[
\sqrt[3]{x\sqrt{x}}
=\sqrt[3]{(\sqrt{x})^3}
=\sqrt{x}
=x^{1/2}.
\]
Taking a cube root undoes cubing a real number. The equivalent expression is therefore \(\boxed{x^{1/2}}\), choice \(\text{D}\).
